/* Room surface materials and their sound absorption coefficients (services/surfaces.js): to describe the room, and so
   the treatment prediction knows the absorption of the finish a product covers. No RT60 is estimated from them, and the
   measurement never uses them. See docs/ROOM-SURFACES.md for how the entries were sourced and checked.

   Each material: id (stable), family and variant (what the screen offers: the family, then the construction), surfaces
   ('wall' | 'floor' | 'ceiling' | 'opening'; a family or category may differ per surface), opening ('door' | 'window' |
   'opening') for materials offered in doorways and windows, alpha at 125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000 Hz (null where the
   source gives no value; never 0 in place of a missing value), source (SOURCES), quality (CLASSES), conditions (what the
   value holds for) and notes.
   - Manufacturer reports to ISO 354 / ISO 11654: alpha is the practical coefficient αp (octave, in 0.05 steps; it can be
     0.00 where the measured value rounds to it). Reports to ASTM C423: the one-third-octave value at the octave centre.
   - Values above 1.00 are kept as printed; they are used limited to 1.00 (as for products).
   - Compiled tables (Acoustical Surfaces, Hall, Vorländer, Sengpiel, Commercial Acoustics, acoustic.ua) largely reproduce
     the same older tables; equal values from several are one entry with the others in its notes, not extra confirmation.
   - Values given per object (sabin per baffle or cloud) are not coefficients and are not included.
   Gathered and checked against the fetched pages and PDFs on 12 October 2026; Rockfon CleanSpace Pro and Ecophon Akusto Wall C
   Extra Bass added on 26 October 2026, checked on the manufacturer's product page and (Ecophon) three of its documents. */
